      "id": "claim_6176e9d47fb740609e42fbd68753f3b8",
      "statement": "The `ulabase.setup.consents.ts` script extends `ulabase.setup.ts` with the consents gate by spreading the accounts steps (minus `appPointsAtService`, kept last) and adding a user schema with `latestConsents`/`consents` fields, a permission allowing users to PATCH their own `consents` (server stamps `latestConsents` and pushes to the `consents` history), JWT claims `latestConsents/tos` and `latestConsents/pp` appended to the `auth` feature's `account-properties-claims` config (there is no separate `/auth-config` endpoint), and a `guards` rule that blocks users who haven't accepted the current ToS/Privacy Policy with HTTP 451.",
